#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073445 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073752 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e79a91b-c479-53da-9f06-59c082fa4187" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Linear Equations Using Substitution"}] :question/id #uuid "e9aae52c-65f3-5dff-bc6b-a530f8c7acc1" :question/math-academy-id "e-13009" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y=4 \\\\ x+2y=16\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. It doesn't matter which equation we pick first, so we choose the easiest one. In this case, the first equation looks like the easiest.\n\nUsing the first equation, we can isolate $x$ by adding $y$ to both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-y & =4 \\\\ x & =4+y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we replace $x$ with $4+y$ in the second equation and solve for $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\tx+2y &=16 \\\n\t(4+y) + 2y &=16\\\n\t4+3y &=16\\\n\t3y &=12\\\n\ty &=4\n}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $y=4$ into $x=4+y$, then we can find the value of $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\tx &= 4 + y \\\n\t   &= 4 + (4) \\\n\t   &=8\n}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x = 8$ and $y = 4$, which can be written as $(8, 4).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073446 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073753 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4352698-7af7-5d74-9c3a-0f951c3e6078" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Challenging System of Linear Equations Using Substitution"}] :question/id #uuid "707504e8-a367-5dc2-a663-371a9dcf7224" :question/math-academy-id "e-13010" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2u+9v-6=0 \\\\ 2u+6v-8=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Sometimes, it's handy to assign a number to each equation in a system, so that we can refer to them more easily:\n![](images/77/77459b19bb1fd1f28e05e6f613e4e49af34595eae33eeeca584d65a289f7ea2c.svg)\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $\\color{blue}(2)$, we can solve for $u$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t2u+6v-8 &= 0 \\\n2u+6v &= 8 \\\n2u &= 8 - 6v \\\nu &= \\dfrac{8-6v}{2} \\\nu &= 4 - 3v\n}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $u=4-3v$ into equation $\\color{red}(1)$ and solve for $v\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t2u+9v-6 &= 0 \\\n\t2(4-3v)+9v-6 &= 0 \\\n\t8-6v+9v-6 &= 0 \\\n2+3v &= 0 \\\n3v &= -2 \\\nv &= -\\dfrac{2}{3}\n}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $v=-\\dfrac{2}{3}$ into equation $\\color{red}(1)$, then we can find the value of $u\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t2u+9v-6 &= 0 \\\n\t2u+9\\left(-\\dfrac{2}{3}\\right) -6 &= 0 \\\n\t2u-6-6 &= 0 \\\n\t2u-12 &= 0 \\\n\t2u &= 12 \\\n\tu &= 6\n}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $u=6$ and $v=-\\dfrac{2}{3}$, which can be written as $\\left(6,-\\dfrac{2}{3}\\right).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496252 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073753 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4352698-7af7-5d74-9c3a-0f951c3e6078" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Challenging System of Linear Equations Using Substitution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ed3f880-96ed-5fd6-824f-be81fbff3e25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495753} {:answer/id #uuid "92cf3e39-98db-564f-a3c5-ad104dff9377" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495833} {:answer/id #uuid "adefce60-eb41-5a32-906f-e3cd671a3daa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495899} {:answer/id #uuid "b6612f39-f352-56c1-817b-399df43c996f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495919} {:answer/id #uuid "e81c2d81-0ae0-51a8-90a5-645bcd295610" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496022}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6ed3f880-96ed-5fd6-824f-be81fbff3e25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495753} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca46e4e1-5150-5d40-98c3-33efe3175aed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496180}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "498d2b3f-6756-59df-bd3d-256bb722b0aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-112214" :question/problem "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $y-x?$\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}21x-9y=0 \\\\ 5y-15x+10=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We number the equations so that we can refer to them more easily:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}21x-9y=0 & \\,\\,(1) \\\\ 5y-15x+10=0 & \\,\\,(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $(2),$ we can isolate $y$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5y-15x+10 & =0 \\\\ 5y & =15x-10 \\\\ y & =3x-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $3x-2$  into equation $(1)$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}21x-9y & =0 \\\\ 21x-9(3x-2) & =0 \\\\ 21x-27x+18 & =0 \\\\ -6x+18 & =0 \\\\ 18 & =6x \\\\ 3 & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $x=3$ into $y=3x-2,$ then we can find the value of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3x-2 \\\\ y & =3(3)-2 \\\\ y & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=3,\\,y=7.$ So,\n\n$$\ny-x=7-3=4.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496226 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073752 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e79a91b-c479-53da-9f06-59c082fa4187" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Linear Equations Using Substitution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51c5dada-d996-51cf-94d1-ca897ceda4c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495696}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51c5dada-d996-51cf-94d1-ca897ceda4c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495696} :answer-field/id #uuid "da300820-d65a-54b5-a122-648e1be4ca42" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496194} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0db68d80-560b-5294-a3e9-812966c11801" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495542}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0db68d80-560b-5294-a3e9-812966c11801" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495542} :answer-field/id #uuid "e16e42d5-5e57-5702-bb36-98fb0bad0dd6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496198}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "07b5302b-d797-5328-827e-aa28a460f929" :question/math-academy-id "q-181149" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}4u-6v=-3 \\\\ u=-v-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the solution $(u,v)$ to this system using the method of substitution.\n\n$(u,v)=($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. It so happens that the second equation is already solved for $u:$\n\n$$\nu=-v-2\n$$\n\nSo, we replace $u$ with $-v-2$ in the first equation and solve for $v:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4u-6v & =-3 \\\\ 4(-v-2)-6v & =-3 \\\\ -4v-8-6v & =-3 \\\\ -10v & =5 \\\\ v & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $v=-\\frac{1}{2}$ into $u=-v-2,$ then we can find the value of $u:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =-v-2 \\\\ u & =-(-\\frac{1}{2})-2 \\\\ u & =-\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $u=-\\frac{3}{2},\\,v=-\\frac{1}{2},$ which can be expressed as $(-\\frac{3}{2},-\\frac{1}{2}).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496255 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073752 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e79a91b-c479-53da-9f06-59c082fa4187" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Linear Equations Using Substitution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "001fa025-6178-5ba4-b287-f99d23255489" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495509}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "001fa025-6178-5ba4-b287-f99d23255489" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495509} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c44ea3f-ae01-5f06-b1d9-d8a1d677d43e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496138} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e2cf528e-9238-53c7-ac72-2595f6c61117" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496013}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e2cf528e-9238-53c7-ac72-2595f6c61117" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496013} :answer-field/id #uuid "d81fe473-caed-55d0-ae06-56890f9a6929" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496191}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4c3907fe-c83e-5bd5-ac54-297aa503451b" :question/math-academy-id "q-181175" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+y=-4 \\\\ x-3y=-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the solution $(x,y)$ to this system using the method of substitution.\n\n$(x,y)=($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. It doesn't matter which equation we pick first, so we choose the easiest one. In this case, the second equation looks like the easiest.\n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $x$ by adding $3y$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\nx=3y-8\n$$\n\nSo, we replace $x$ with $3y-8$ in the first equation and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x+y & =-4 \\\\ -2(3y-8)+y & =-4 \\\\ -6y+16+y & =-4 \\\\ -5y & =-20 \\\\ y & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $y=4$ into $x=3y-8,$ then we can find the value of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =3y-8 \\\\ x & =3(4)-8 \\\\ x & =12-8 \\\\ x & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=4,\\,y=4,$ which can be expressed as $(4,4).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496314 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073753 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4352698-7af7-5d74-9c3a-0f951c3e6078" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Challenging System of Linear Equations Using Substitution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff409c69-65be-5db8-9082-449cc256ae35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496070}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff409c69-65be-5db8-9082-449cc256ae35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496070} :answer-field/id #uuid "d502feb6-12a4-5b5d-a239-789af82850e4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496187} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be1f5640-6243-5fce-a7c7-5b82c5d69ef4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495929}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be1f5640-6243-5fce-a7c7-5b82c5d69ef4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495929} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef8a675b-4a10-5910-adfc-f84ccbe5facf" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496207}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d389f84f-6df2-5d57-9702-acb625d9c80f" :question/math-academy-id "q-181207" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3p-6q=-18 \\\\ 4p+3q+2=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the solution $(p,q)$ to this system using the method of substitution.\n\n$(p,q)=($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$" :question/worked-solution "We number the equations so that we can refer to them more easily:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3p-6q=-18 & \\,\\,(1) \\\\ 4p+3q+2=0 & \\,\\,(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $(1),$ we can solve for $p$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3p-6q & =-18 \\\\ 3p & =6q-18 \\\\ p & =2q-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $p=2q-6$ into equation $(2)$ and solve for $q:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(2q-6)+3q+2 & =0 \\\\ 8q-24+3q+2 & =0 \\\\ 11q & =22 \\\\ q & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $q=2$ into equation $(1),$ then we can find the value of $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3p-6(2) & =-18 \\\\ 3p-12 & =-18 \\\\ 3p & =-6 \\\\ p & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $p=-2,\\,q=2,$ which can be expressed as $(-2,2).$"}]}
